/*Q11.
Liam, a data scientist, is developing a data compression algorithm that leverages bit wise right-shifting as a crucial step. In the compression process, integers are represented in a compressed form. To reconstruct the original data efficiently, Liam needs a program that performs the right shift operation on the compressed data. Can you help Liam by writing a Java program that takes the compressed data and the number of positions to right-shift, then outputs the recovered original data?

Input format:
  - The first line is the integer that represents compressed data.
  - The second line is the integer that represents the number of positions to right-shift.

Output format:
  - The output is the integer that represents the shifted value.

Note: A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: >> is the signed right shift (it preserves the sign for negatives).*/
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int data = sc.nextInt();
        int positions = sc.nextInt();
        System.out.println(data >> positions);
        sc.close();
    }
}
